      "content": "2. THE CORE PRINCIPLE — ENGLISH PREFERS CLARITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "English fundamentally favors clarity, conciseness, and directness over overly complex structures.",
        "In Subject-Verb Agreement, always identify the real subject by ignoring intervening descriptive clauses.",
        "Elimination is your most powerful tool to quickly weed out grammatically incorrect or redundant options.",
        "A sentence may be grammatically correct but logically wrong; context and meaning must always be verified.",
        "Maintain strict parallel structure and avoid redundant expressions or double comparatives."
